---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { LinkButton } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import josue from '../assets/team/josue.jpg';
import adriano from '../assets/team/adriano.jpg';
import hotDipStation from '../assets/problem/hot-dip-station.jpg';
import cadPerspective from '../assets/proposal/cad/cad-perspective.png';
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Safe Dip',
		template: 'splash',
	}}
	hasSidebar={false}
>
	<div class="landing">
		<section class="hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">Valencia College &middot; ECET Senior Design Capstone</p>
			<h1>Safe Dip</h1>
			<p class="tagline">Automated Safety for Hot Dip Coating</p>
			<p class="lede">
				An automated pick-and-place system that dips metal components into hot wax
				baths without a worker needing to be in direct contact with the process.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<LinkButton href="/proposal/report-and-presentation/" icon="right-arrow">
					Read the Proposal
				</LinkButton>
				<LinkButton href="/about/" variant="minimal">Meet the Team</LinkButton>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>The Problem</h2>
			<p>
				Hot-dipping processes are used in manufacturing to coat, treat, or finish
				parts. However, manual operation near heated baths can expose workers to
				safety risks such as burns, repetitive strain, and inconsistent handling.
			</p>
			<p>
				This project addresses the need for a safer and more controlled way to
				move metal parts through a dipping process. By automating the pickup,
				dipping, and unloading sequence, Safe Dip aims to reduce the amount of
				time an operator spends near the hot wax bath.
			</p>

			<figure class="figure">
				<Image
					src={hotDipStation}
					alt="A heated wax pot on a rolling cart beside trays of metal parts waiting to be dipped by hand"
					widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
					sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 56rem, 92vw"
				/>
				<figcaption>
					The process today: a heated wax pot and the parts staged beside it, each
					one loaded and retrieved by hand.
				</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>Existing Solutions</h2>
			<p class="block-lede">
				A short, honest look at how this problem is handled today — and where each
				approach falls short.
			</p>
			<div class="compare-grid">
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h3>Manual dipping</h3>
					<p>
						<strong>Cost:</strong> low equipment cost, high ongoing labor cost.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Limitations:</strong> direct burn/chemical exposure risk;
						dwell time and immersion depth vary operator to operator.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h3>Dip-spin machines (EFFCO DS-250, MS800)</h3>
					<p><strong>Cost:</strong> $15k–$80k.</p>
					<p><strong>Limitations:</strong> batch-only — no individual part handling, no pick-and-place, and manual basket loading/unloading.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h3>Single-purpose fastener coaters</h3>
					<p><strong>Cost:</strong> $3k–$30k.</p>
					<p><strong>Limitations:</strong> fixed to one chemical and one fastener geometry; no pick-and-place or variable dip depth.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h3>Full robotic dip cells (Emmeti WAX-ON, South Shore)</h3>
					<p><strong>Cost:</strong> $50k–$150k+.</p>
					<p><strong>Limitations:</strong> true pick-and-place and variable depth, but priced and sized for industrial lines, not small-scale or research use.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="compare-more"><a href="/proposal/comparable-products/">Full comparison, product-by-product →</a></p>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>Our Solution</h2>
			<p>
				The proposed solution is a small automated <strong>pick-and-place</strong>
				system — a mechanism that picks up a part from one fixed location and
				places it at another, following a repeatable, programmed motion path —
				designed to move metallic components through a hot wax dipping process.
				The system is expected to:
			</p>
			<ol class="sequence">
				<li>Detect or receive a part from an input area.</li>
				<li>Pick up the part using an electromagnet.</li>
				<li>Move the part horizontally over the wax container.</li>
				<li>Lower the part into the wax using a vertical motion system.</li>
				<li>Raise the part after the dipping step.</li>
				<li>Move the part to an output area.</li>
				<li>Release the part safely.</li>
				<li>Stop operation through an emergency stop system when needed.</li>
			</ol>

			<figure class="figure">
				<Image
					src={cadPerspective}
					alt="CAD render of the Safe Dip two-axis Cartesian gantry, showing the horizontal beam, vertical assembly, and dipping station"
					widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
					sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 56rem, 92vw"
				/>
				<figcaption>
					The proposed design: a two-axis Cartesian gantry that carries the part
					between the input station, the dipping bath, and the output station.
					See <a href="/proposal/cad/">CAD Drawings &amp; Renderings</a> for
					dimensions and further views.
				</figcaption>
			</figure>

			<h3 class="sub">System at a Glance</h3>
			<p class="block-lede">
				Safe Dip breaks down into seven subsystems that coordinate to run the
				load&ndash;dip&ndash;unload cycle:
			</p>
			<div class="compare-grid">
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h4>Processing Module</h4>
					<p>Controls the logic of the system and coordinates sensors, motors, and the electromagnet.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h4>Sensing Module</h4>
					<p>Detects part position, system status, or movement limits.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h4>Movement Module</h4>
					<p>Controls horizontal and vertical motion.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h4>Electromagnetic End-Effector</h4>
					<p>Picks up and releases metallic parts.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h4>Power Distribution Module</h4>
					<p>Supplies power to motors, controller, sensors, and the electromagnet.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h4>Communication Module</h4>
					<p>Allows the system to send or receive information from a computer or interface.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="compare-card">
					<h4>Emergency Stop Module</h4>
					<p>Provides a safety shutdown method during abnormal operation.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>Project Objectives</h2>
			<ul class="objectives">
				<li><strong>Low cost</strong> — maintain a low-cost design compared to industrial robotic systems.</li>
				<li><strong>Safety</strong> — improve safety by reducing manual handling near hot wax.</li>
				<li><strong>Autonomy</strong> — automate the load&ndash;dip&ndash;unload process.</li>
				<li><strong>Electromagnetic handling</strong> — use an electromagnet to pick up metallic parts.</li>
				<li><strong>Controlled dipping</strong> — control vertical dipping depth.</li>
				<li><strong>Repeatable motion</strong> — move the part between input, wax bath, and output positions.</li>
				<li><strong>Fail-safe operation</strong> — include emergency stop functionality.</li>
				<li><strong>Modularity</strong> — keep the design modular and suitable for a Senior Design prototype.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>Project Status</h2>
			<p class="block-lede">Where the project stands right now.</p>
			<ol class="phases">
				<li>
					<strong>Concept Development</strong> — identified the safety problem
					related to manual hot-dipping processes and proposed an automated
					pick-and-place solution.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Initial System Architecture</strong> — divided the project into
					major subsystems: sensing, processing, motion, end-effector,
					communication, power distribution, and emergency stop.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>End-Effector Direction</strong> — changed direction from a
					mechanical claw concept to an electromagnetic pickup concept for
					metallic tools or parts.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Research &amp; Proposal Development</strong> — researching
					feasibility, safety considerations, and technical requirements needed
					to complete the proposal.
				</li>
				<li class="phase-future">
					<strong>Future Work</strong> — CAD models, wiring diagrams, control
					logic, component selection, test results, and final prototype
					documentation.
				</li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>Glossary</h2>
			<dl class="glossary">
				<div class="glossary-item">
					<dt>Pick-and-place</dt>
					<dd>A mechanism that automatically picks up an object from one location and places it at another along a repeatable path.</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="glossary-item">
					<dt>Block diagram</dt>
					<dd>A system-level drawing that shows each subsystem as a labeled box, with arrows showing how power, data, or signals flow between them.</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="glossary-item">
					<dt>Power budget</dt>
					<dd>A tally of how much current every component in the system draws, organized by voltage rail, used to size the power supply correctly.</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="glossary-item">
					<dt>Dwell time</dt>
					<dd>How long a part is held submerged in the dip bath before being raised back out.</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="glossary-item">
					<dt>End effector</dt>
					<dd>The part of the mechanism that directly contacts the workpiece — here, an electromagnet that picks up and releases the metal part being dipped.</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="glossary-item">
					<dt>E-stop (emergency stop)</dt>
					<dd>A dedicated button that immediately cuts power to the system's motors, used to halt motion in an unsafe situation.</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>Team</h2>
			<div class="team-grid">
				<a class="team-card" href="/about/">
					<Image src={josue} alt="" width={144} densities={[1, 2]} />
					<h3>Josué Bouchard</h3>
					<p class="role">Embedded Firmware &amp; Controls</p>
					<p class="bio">Studied Computer Engineering at Universidad de Buenos Aires before transferring to Valencia College; aiming toward embedded systems, aerospace, or robotics.</p>
				</a>
				<a class="team-card" href="/about/">
					<Image src={adriano} alt="" width={144} densities={[1, 2]} />
					<h3>Adriano Duque Mena</h3>
					<p class="role">Mechanical Design &amp; Assembly</p>
					<p class="bio">Born in Colón, Matanzas, Cuba; transitioned from Aerospace Engineering to Electrical &amp; Computer Engineering Technology at Valencia College.</p>
				</a>
			</div>
			<p class="team-link"><a href="/about/">Full team page →</a></p>
		</section>
	</div>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
	.landing {
		max-width: 60rem;
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding-inline: 1rem;
	}

	.hero {
		text-align: center;
		padding-block: 3rem 2.5rem;
	}
	.eyebrow {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
	}
	.hero h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.tagline {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
		color: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
		font-weight: 600;
		margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
	}
	.lede {
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin: 0 auto 1.75rem;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
	}
	.cta-row {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		justify-content: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}

	.block {
		padding-block: 2.25rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-6);
	}
	.block h2 {
		margin-top: 0;
		margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
		line-height: 1.25;
	}
	.block-lede {
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		margin-top: 0;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.figure {
		margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
	}
	.figure :global(img) {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		background: var(--sl-color-bg-nav);
	}
	.figure figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.65rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		line-height: 1.5;
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.sequence {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
		gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.sequence li {
		padding-block: 0.15rem;
	}

	.sub {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
		line-height: 1.25;
	}

	.phases {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
		counter-reset: phase;
	}
	.phases li {
		counter-increment: phase;
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem 0.75rem 2.75rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-bg-nav);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--sl-color-accent);
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
		position: relative;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.phases li::before {
		content: counter(phase);
		position: absolute;
		left: 0.9rem;
		top: 0.75rem;
		width: 1.35rem;
		height: 1.35rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--sl-color-accent);
		color: var(--sl-color-bg);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		font-weight: 700;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
	}
	.phases li.phase-future {
		opacity: 0.7;
		border-left-style: dashed;
	}

	.compare-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
	}
	.compare-card {
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-bg-nav);
	}
	.compare-card h3,
	.compare-card h4 {
		margin-top: 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
	}
	.compare-card--todo {
		opacity: 0.6;
		border-style: dashed;
	}

	.objectives {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
		gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
	}
	.objectives li {
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-bg-nav);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--sl-color-accent);
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
	}

	.glossary {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
		gap: 1.25rem 2rem;
		margin: 0;
	}
	.glossary-item dt {
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.glossary-item dd {
		margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}

	.team-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr));
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}
	.team-card {
		display: block;
		text-decoration: none;
		color: inherit;
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 1.25rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-bg-nav);
		transition: border-color 0.15s ease;
	}
	.team-card:hover {
		border-color: var(--sl-color-accent);
	}
	.team-card img {
		width: 4.5rem;
		height: 4.5rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		object-fit: cover;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}
	.team-card h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.15rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
	}
	.team-card .role {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
		color: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
	}
	.team-card .bio {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}
	.team-link,
	.compare-more {
		text-align: center;
		margin-top: 1.25rem;
	}
</style>
